🔥 10 BIGGEST LESSONS

1️⃣ Humans dominate through cooperation

Our greatest advantage isn't physical strength. It's our ability to cooperate in huge numbers.

2️⃣ Stories shape civilizations

Nations, money, corporations and religions depend heavily on shared beliefs.

3️⃣ Technology changes behavior

Technology doesn't simply serve humans. Humans reorganize their lives around technology.

4️⃣ Progress isn't always simple

A development can improve one aspect of life while making another worse.

5️⃣ Money depends on trust

Economic systems ultimately require collective confidence.

6️⃣ Writing amplified human memory

It allowed civilizations to store and process information beyond individual brains.

7️⃣ Science begins with admitting ignorance

You don't need to know everything. You need to be willing to discover what you don't know.

8️⃣ Large systems require shared rules

Millions of strangers can cooperate because they follow common systems.

9️⃣ History is interconnected

Technology, economics, politics, culture and biology continuously influence one another.

🔟 AI may become another major historical turning point

Humanity may be approaching a transition as significant as previous technological revolutions.


---

💡 THE BIGGEST LESSON FOR YOU

Given your technology/AI learning journey, I want you to pay particular attention to this:

Don't only learn technology.

Learn how technology changes humans and society.

A great AI engineer understands:

Code → Data → Algorithms → People → Organizations → Society

That is much broader than simply knowing how to build a model.

If you understand both technology and human behavior, you become much better equipped to think about the consequences—and opportunities—of AI.


